{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-03-13","source":"Senate","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Commerce, Science, and Transportation.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"10000","actionDate":"2025-03-13","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in Senate","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/1017","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001098","fullName":"Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"S001198","fullName":"Sen. Sullivan, Dan [R-AK]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AK"},{"bioguideId":"B001305","fullName":"Sen. Budd, Ted [R-NC]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"C001047","fullName":"Sen. Capito, Shelley Moore [R-WV]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WV"},{"bioguideId":"B001243","fullName":"Sen. Blackburn, Marsha [R-TN]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"Y000064","fullName":"Sen. Young, Todd [R-IN]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"F000463","fullName":"Sen. Fischer, Deb [R-NE]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NE"},{"bioguideId":"L000571","fullName":"Sen. Lummis, Cynthia M. [R-WY]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WY"},{"bioguideId":"M001242","fullName":"Sen. Moreno, Bernie [R-OH]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-06-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T05:58:11+00:00","id":"s1017-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-13","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Commerce, Science, and Transportation."},"laws":[],"number":"1017","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Transportation and Public Works","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"S001232","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Sheehy, Tim [R-MT]","party":"R","state":"MT"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-13","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Safe and Secure Transportation of American Energy Act</strong></p><p>This bill expands the types of activities that are subject to criminal penalties related to damaging or destroying an interstate gas or hazardous liquid pipeline facility.</p><p>Under current law, a person who knowingly and willfully damages or destroys a pipeline facility is subject to criminal penalties, including a&nbsp;fine, a prison term of up to 20 years, or both. If a death&nbsp;results from the offense, the person may be imprisoned for any term of years or life.&nbsp;</p><p>Under the bill, these criminal penalties also apply to a person who knowingly and willfully</p><ul><li>vandalizes,</li><li>tampers with, or</li><li>disrupts or prevents the operation or construction of the facility.</li></ul>","updateDate":"2025-08-13T14:36:56Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Safe and Secure Transportation of American Energy Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-09-08T18:03:40Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-08T18:03:40Z"}
